<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Cenel nGabrain</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 850 CE (approx.) · capital Dunadd</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The dominant kindred of Dal Riata in Kintyre, whose kings, from Aedan mac Gabrain onwards, most often held the overkingship of Gaelic Argyll.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cenel nGabrain traced its descent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabran-mac-domangairt">Gabran</a>, said to be a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergus-mor">Fergus Mor</a>, and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kintyre">Kintyre</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Arran</a> and nearby lands in the 6th century. Its leading king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Aedan mac Gabrain</a>, was ordained by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba of Iona</a> according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adomnan">Adomnan</a>, and campaigned widely in northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> before his defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria">Aethelfrith</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-bernicia">Bernicia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-degsastan">Degsastan</a> in 603.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kindred controlled the hillfort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunadd">Dunadd</a> for much of its history and competed with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cenel-loairn">Cenel Loairn</a> for the overkingship. Its rulers patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a> and fought both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britons-celtic-people">Britons</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-strathclyde">Alt Clut</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senchus-fer-n-alban">Senchus fer nAlban</a> records its houses and duties to supply ships.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-moira">Mag Rath</a> in 637 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domnall-brecc">Domnall Brecc</a>, and later Pictish conquest, eroded its standing. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenneth-macalpin">Kenneth MacAlpin</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland</a> in the 840s, was traditionally counted among its descendants, giving the kindred a central place in Scottish royal genealogy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cenel-ngabrain.jpg" alt="Cenel nGabrain" width="320" height="337"><figcaption>Image: User:Hogweard · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argyll_-_Knapdale.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 850 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dunadd</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aedan mac Gabrain, Domnall Brecc, Eochaid Buide</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cenél nGabráin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=cenel-ngabrain" aria-label="Cenel nGabrain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4561 268 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cenel nGabrain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4881 524L4881 524"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 524h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4881 524h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4881 524h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dunadd. <a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=cenel-ngabrain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

